<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <aside class="prose-rail">Use case 07 / 08</aside>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>Premium services are easy to default to and hard to audit. IL identifies shipments that consistently arrive faster than the service they were paid for — and the lanes where a slower, cheaper mode would meet customer commitments just as well.</p>

        <figure class="uc-screenshot"><img src="../../assets/uc-07-analysis.png" alt="Service level and mode analysis — IL screenshot"></figure>

        <div class="uc-twocol">
          <div class="uc-col">
            <h4>What IL helps you do</h4>
            <ul><li>Identify shipments that could move on a slower, lower-cost service</li><li>Surface mode mismatches across parcel, LTL, and freight</li><li>Track effective discount and net charge by service and lane</li><li>Quantify the savings of right-sizing service mix</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="uc-col">
            <h4>Business impact</h4>
            <ul><li>Reduce overspend on premium services that aren't required</li><li>Right-size mode selection based on real delivery patterns</li><li>Improve carrier scorecards with hard service-level data</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Why teams adopt this <em>first</em>.</h3>
        <p>Mode analysis is the highest-leverage report for shippers running mixed-mode networks. The savings show up in the next billing cycle, not next year.</p>

        <div class="uc-pager">
          <a class="prev" href="../exceptions-monitoring/index.html">
            <span class="label">← Previous · 06</span>
            <span class="title">Exceptions <em>monitoring</em></span>
          </a>
